# Project Specification

Saved on: 2024-08-28

## Basics
- **Project Name:** E-commerce API response validator — test 3 implementations
- **Goal:** Run 3 E-commerce API implementations and compare pass rates + latency
- **Test Type:** B (3 different branches/implementations)

## Tech Stack
- **Runtime:** Node.js 20 LTS
- **Framework:** Express.js
- **Testing:** Jest
- **Database:** PostgreSQL 15
- **Package Manager:** npm v9

## Repository
- **Owner:** PatericTy
- **Repo:** ecommerce-test-harness
- **Branches under test:**
  - `impl-a`
  - `impl-b`
  - `impl-c`
- **Default branch:** main

## Environment
- **OS:** Linux
- **Containerization:** Docker Desktop
- **Services:** PostgreSQL 15 (containerized)

## Metrics & Scoring
- **Primary Metric:** Pass Rate (% of tests passing)
- **Secondary Metric:** Latency (test execution time in ms)
- **Score Formula:** `0.7 * (pass_rate / 100) + 0.3 * (1 - latency / 500)`
- **Tie-Breaker:** Lower latency preferred
- **Max Latency Threshold:** 500ms (normalization constant)

## Acceptance Criteria
✅ **PASS** if BOTH:
1. Pass Rate ≥ 95%
2. Latency < 250ms

❌ **FAIL** if either threshold is not met

## Deliverables (All ✅)
- [x] Scaffold project files
- [x] Test harness script (`run-tests.sh`)
- [x] Example tests (Jest suite)
- [x] GitHub Actions workflow
- [x] README with run instructions
- [x] Comprehensive documentation (`docs/HARNESS.md`)

## Commands
- **Local harness:** `./run-tests.sh`
- **Install deps:** `npm ci`
- **Run tests:** `npm test`
- **Unit tests:** `npm run test:unit`
- **Integration tests:** `npm run test:integration`

## CI/CD
- **Platform:** GitHub Actions
- **Trigger:** Push to main / impl-a / impl-b / impl-c, PR to main
- **Secrets Required:**
  - `DB_PASSWORD`
  - `API_KEY`
- **Artifacts:** `test-results.json`
- **PR Comments:** Yes (summary of best implementation)

## Priority
**Reliability** — Pass rate weighted at 70% of overall score

## Data & Fixtures
- Test fixtures: `fixtures/products-list.json` (example)
- Expected responses: Fixtures follow standard JSON structure
- External data: https://example.com/test-fixtures.zip (to be integrated)

## Additional Notes
- Tag @PatericTy on PRs
- Use Node 20 LTS only
- Prefer lower latency for tie-breaking
- Database runs in Docker container during CI

